  "liner": {
   "body_md": "## Setlist highlights\n\n- **banter - some old school Soulive**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n- **banter - bringing up the Shady Horns**: earliest performance in the archive; mythic rare: 2 archived performances [4]\n- **Got Soul**: rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **Drum solo**: rare: 10 archived performances [4]\n- **banter - thanks**: earliest performance in the archive; legendary: the only archived performance [4]\n\n## The recordings\n\n- **soulive2011-06-03.tlm170.flac16** (recommended): audience recording; 13 songs; 74 min [1]. Said about its sound: Very windy day; wind gusts are audible despite foam windscreens on the microphones; Uploader applied targeted low-shelf filtering in SoundForge starting around 400Hz to reduce wind rumble, across many tracks [1]\n- **soulive2011-06-03.akg481.flac24**: source not stated; 8 songs; 72 min [2]\n- **soulive2011-06-03.akg481.flac16**: source not stated; 8 songs; 72 min [3]\n\n## Around the show\n\n- Shady Horns joined on some songs: Ryan Zoidas on sax and Brian Thomas on trombone [1]\n- Taper credits Corey for providing the clamp space for the microphones [2]\n\n## Tapers and lineage\n\n- **soulive2011-06-03.tlm170.flac16**: taped by Scott Bernstein; transferred by Scott Bernstein; source: Audience [1]. Also: Recorded with a TLM170 microphone, mastered and tracked by Scott Bernstein; FLAC 16-bit [1]\n- **soulive2011-06-03.akg481.flac24**: taped by vanark; transferred by vanark; source: AKG C480B/CK61 > Edirol UA-5 (Oade Warm+ mod) > Edirol R-09HR (24/48) [2]. Also: This is a separate AKG 481 recording, released as a 24-bit FLAC set, not meant for CD-Audio [2]\n- **soulive2011-06-03.akg481.flac16**: taped by vanark; transferred by vanark; source: AKG C480B/CK61 > Edirol UA-5 (Oade Warm+ mod) > Edirol R-09HR (24/48) [3]",
